# Copy to .env and uncomment/edit what you need — .gitignore already
# excludes .env (but not this file). internal/dotenv.Load() reads it from
# the working directory as the very first thing cmd/nexusd, cmd/signerd,
# cmd/nexusctl, and evals/cmd/runner do, before anything else in those
# binaries reads an environment variable.
#
# A real environment variable always wins over this file — `FOO=bar make
# run` (or CI's/a deploy's own env) is never shadowed by a stale .env. A
# missing .env is not an error either: every variable below has always
# worked, and keeps working, via a plain shell export with no .env file at
# all (docs/local-llm.md's Setup sections use exactly that style). This
# file exists purely so you don't have to retype the same long export
# lines on every restart.
#
# Everything here is commented out with its actual default value shown —
# uncomment only what you want to override. Values are NOT quoted unless
# the value itself needs to contain a literal # or leading/trailing space.

# --- nexusd: core server (cmd/nexusd/config.go) ---
# Outside --dev, every one of these five is REQUIRED (loadServerConfig
# fails fast, listing everything missing, rather than starting against a
# localhost default no real deployment intends). --dev fills in the
# zero-setup defaults shown below instead.
# NEXUS_DATABASE_URL=postgres://nexus_app:nexus_app@localhost:6432/nexus
# NEXUS_ADMIN_DATABASE_URL=postgres://nexus:nexus@localhost:5433/nexus
# NEXUS_MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL=postgres://nexus:nexus@localhost:5433/nexus
# NEXUS_REDIS_ADDR=localhost:6380
# NEXUS_SIGNERD_SOCKET=.dev/signerd.sock
# NEXUS_KEK_PATH=.dev/kek.key
# NEXUS_AUTHN_SIGNING_KEY_PATH=.dev/authn_signing.key
# NEXUS_HTTP_ADDR=:8055

# --- nexusd: queue backend (docs/build-phases.md Phase 18) ---
# redis (default, a Redis Streams consumer group) | postgres (the original
# SKIP LOCKED adapter, kept as a one-env-var rollback)
# NEXUS_QUEUE_BACKEND=redis

# --- nexusd: model provider (cmd/nexusd's newProvider) ---
# fake (default, --dev's own scripted/no-network provider) | anthropic | litellm
# NEXUS_PROVIDER=fake
# NEXUS_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# NEXUS_LITELLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4100
# NEXUS_LITELLM_MODEL=qwen2.5-local
# NEXUS_LITELLM_API_KEY=

# --- nexusd: tracing (docs/local-llm.md, docs/observability.md) — any
# ONE of the three blocks below works alone; NEXUS_OTLP_ENDPOINT (blocks 1
# or 2) and NEXUS_LANGFUSE_HOST (block 3) can ALSO both be set at once —
# newSpanExporter fans out to both simultaneously via obs.MultiExporter
# (internal/obs/multi.go), each correctly nested independently, e.g. Tempo
# + langfuse-lite receiving the same run's spans at the same time. Nothing
# set means spans print to stdout as NDJSON (the zero-setup default,
# nothing to bring up first).

# 1) OTLP against Grafana Tempo (generic tracing, correlated in the SAME
#    Grafana `make observability-up` runs: `make tempo-up`) — no headers or
#    non-default URL path needed, unlike Langfuse's OTLP endpoint below.
# NEXUS_OTLP_ENDPOINT=localhost:4418

# 2) OTLP against the full 6-container self-hosted Langfuse (`make langfuse-up`)
# NEXUS_OTLP_ENDPOINT=localhost:3001
# NEXUS_OTLP_URL_PATH=/api/public/otel/v1/traces
# NEXUS_OTLP_HEADERS=Authorization=Basic cGstbGYtYzBiNWVhMmY2ZmI4OTkwZDFmNTkyMTVlNWY3OWMxNjM6c2stbGYtMWNlMTc2Mjk2Nzk5MGFhY2JmZjU3Yzg5NGNlYTZlMzk=
# NEXUS_OTLP_INSECURE=true

# 3) Native Langfuse ingestion (the lightweight 2-container self-hosted
#    Langfuse v2: `make langfuse-lite-up`) — internal/obs/langfuse.go
# NEXUS_LANGFUSE_HOST=http://localhost:3001
# NEXUS_LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-c0b5ea2f6fb8990d1f59215e5f79c163
# NEXUS_LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-1ce1762967990aacbff57c894cea6e39

# Opt-in only, either tracing path above: attach real prompt/completion/
# tool input-output to spans (constitution Principle VI's sanctioned
# exception) — off means telemetry stays content-free by construction.
# NEXUS_TRACE_CONTENT=false

# --- nexusd: tool sandboxing (cmd/nexusd's newSandboxFactory) ---
# unset (default, platform/shell runs unsandboxed) | docker | opensandbox
# NEXUS_SANDBOX=
# NEXUS_OPENSANDBOX_URL=http://localhost:8090
# NEXUS_OPENSANDBOX_API_KEY=nexus-dev-opensandbox-key
# NEXUS_CRAWL4AI_URL=http://localhost:11235
# NEXUS_CRAWL4AI_API_TOKEN=nexus-dev-crawl4ai-token
# comma-separated hostnames platform/web_fetch may reach; empty = none allowed
# NEXUS_WEB_FETCH_ALLOWLIST=

# --- nexusd: storage roots + skills signing ---
# NEXUS_WORKSPACE_ROOT=.dev/workspaces
# NEXUS_BLOB_DIR=.dev/blobs
# NEXUS_MEMORY_ROOT=.dev/memory
# NEXUS_SKILLS_ROOT=skills
# NEXUS_SKILLS_SIGNING_PUBKEY=

# --- nexusd: OAuth connectors (internal/connectors, README task 11.2) ---
# NEXUS_OAUTH_PROVIDERS is a comma-separated list of names; each name then
# needs its own NEXUS_OAUTH_<NAME>_* set (shown here for a placeholder
# provider called EXAMPLE — repeat the block, one per name in the list
# above, using each provider's own credentials).
# NEXUS_OAUTH_PROVIDERS=
# NEXUS_OAUTH_EXAMPLE_CLIENT_ID=
# NEXUS_OAUTH_EXAMPLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# NEXUS_OAUTH_EXAMPLE_AUTH_URL=
# NEXUS_OAUTH_EXAMPLE_TOKEN_URL=
# NEXUS_OAUTH_EXAMPLE_REDIRECT_URL=
# NEXUS_OAUTH_EXAMPLE_SCOPES=

# --- nexusd + signerd: logging (internal/obs.InitLogger) ---
# trace|debug|info|warn|error — an unparseable value falls back to info
# NEXUS_LOG_LEVEL=info
# additionally tee JSON logs to this path (Promtail tails these, docs/observability.md)
# NEXUS_LOG_FILE=.dev/nexusd.log

# --- signerd (cmd/signerd/main.go) ---
# NEXUS_SIGNER_KEY_PATH=.dev/signer/ed25519.key

# --- nexusctl (internal/surfaces/cli) ---
# NEXUS_HTTP_ADDR=http://localhost:8055
# mint one with `make token` (TENANT=name make token for a non-default tenant)
# NEXUS_TOKEN=

# --- eval runner (evals/cmd/runner, Makefile's `eval`/`eval-baseline`) ---
# NEXUS_REGION=local
# NEXUS_LIVEEVAL_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
